1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:00,735
Hello!

2
00:00:00,735 --> 00:00:06,466
In this final week, you will plan your exam day, review your personal mistakes,

3
00:00:06,466 --> 00:00:10,020
and learn how to read your mock results sensibly.

4
00:00:11,320 --> 00:00:12,286
Strategy one:

5
00:00:12,286 --> 00:00:15,928
for test-room rules, trust only official sources.

6
00:00:15,928 --> 00:00:18,530
This app does not list those rules.

7
00:00:18,530 --> 00:00:24,624
Read your registration confirmation carefully, check the test organiser's website,

8
00:00:24,624 --> 00:00:28,192
and ask your test centre if anything is unclear.

9
00:00:29,492 --> 00:00:33,140
Could you confirm what identification I need to bring?

10
00:00:36,440 --> 00:00:41,036
The final week is for consolidating, not for learning new material.

11
00:00:41,036 --> 00:00:44,603
Review your vocabulary and your personal error list,

12
00:00:44,603 --> 00:00:47,964
and take a mock test in your real exam time slot.

13
00:00:47,964 --> 00:00:51,256
The day before the exam, do only a light review,

14
00:00:51,256 --> 00:00:57,224
prepare what your confirmation letter asks for, check your route, and get enough sleep.

15
00:00:58,524 --> 00:00:59,455
Strategy two:

16
00:00:59,455 --> 00:01:01,029
Listening and Reading.

17
00:01:01,029 --> 00:01:05,252
Listening takes about thirty minutes, with forty questions:

18
00:01:05,252 --> 00:01:09,761
use the reading time to look ahead, and circle the word limits.

19
00:01:09,761 --> 00:01:11,766
Reading takes sixty minutes:

20
00:01:11,766 --> 00:01:15,344
about seventeen, twenty, and twenty-three minutes,

21
00:01:15,344 --> 00:01:18,780
and in the last two minutes fill in every blank.

22
00:01:20,080 --> 00:01:24,256
A blank scores nothing, so I'll write my best option.

23
00:01:27,556 --> 00:01:28,679
Strategy three:

24
00:01:28,679 --> 00:01:30,401
Writing, sixty minutes.

25
00:01:30,401 --> 00:01:34,743
If you do Task 1 first, aim to finish it by minute twenty,

26
00:01:34,743 --> 00:01:38,261
and start checking Task 2 at minute fifty-five.

27
00:01:38,261 --> 00:01:43,876
Choose an order you have practised, and don't change it at the last minute.

28
00:01:45,176 --> 00:01:49,138
Overall, the car remained the most common way to commute,

29
00:01:49,138 --> 00:01:51,848
but its share fell sharply in one city.

30
00:01:55,148 --> 00:01:59,262
In conclusion, I believe the benefits outweigh the drawbacks,

31
00:01:59,262 --> 00:02:02,972
as long as employers keep regular face-to-face contact.

32
00:02:06,272 --> 00:02:07,278
Strategy four:

33
00:02:07,278 --> 00:02:10,725
Speaking takes about eleven to fourteen minutes.

34
00:02:10,725 --> 00:02:15,251
Speak naturally, extend your answers with reasons and examples,

35
00:02:15,251 --> 00:02:17,190
and don't memorise answers.

36
00:02:17,190 --> 00:02:22,792
If you didn't hear a question clearly, politely ask the examiner to repeat it.

37
00:02:22,792 --> 00:02:26,240
That is better than guessing the wrong question.

38
00:02:27,540 --> 00:02:31,308
Sorry, could you repeat the question, please?

39
00:02:34,608 --> 00:02:36,830
How to read your mock results.

40
00:02:36,830 --> 00:02:42,457
The Listening and Reading bands are based on the app's own conversion table.

41
00:02:42,457 --> 00:02:48,455
The Writing band uses the formula Task 1 plus two times Task 2, divided by three,

42
00:02:48,455 --> 00:02:51,269
rounded down to the nearest half band.

43
00:02:51,269 --> 00:02:54,083
This is an estimate, not a real score.

44
00:02:54,083 --> 00:02:58,896
For any skill below seven point zero, add two to four more weeks.

45
00:03:00,196 --> 00:03:01,286
Common mistakes:

46
00:03:01,286 --> 00:03:07,074
believing rumours about test-room rules, studying new material late the night before,

47
00:03:07,074 --> 00:03:11,908
leaving blanks when time runs out, and writing Task 1 with no overview.

48
00:03:13,208 --> 00:03:14,990
Mini quiz, question one.

49
00:03:14,990 --> 00:03:21,152
Where should you check the test-room rules, to be sure the information is reliable?

50
00:03:24,452 --> 00:03:25,653
Question two.

51
00:03:25,653 --> 00:03:30,641
In Reading, you have two minutes left and four blanks.

52
00:03:30,641 --> 00:03:32,396
What should you do?

53
00:03:35,696 --> 00:03:36,929
Question three.

54
00:03:36,929 --> 00:03:41,037
In Speaking, you didn't hear the question clearly.

55
00:03:41,037 --> 00:03:42,680
What should you say?

56
00:03:42,680 --> 00:03:46,952
Try saying it in English before you hear the answer.

57
00:03:50,252 --> 00:03:50,898
Answers.

58
00:03:50,898 --> 00:03:51,221
One:

59
00:03:51,221 --> 00:03:56,792
your confirmation letter, the official website, and your test centre.

60
00:03:56,792 --> 00:03:57,115
Two:

61
00:03:57,115 --> 00:04:01,152
fill in all four with the most reasonable options.

62
00:04:01,152 --> 00:04:01,636
Three:

63
00:04:01,636 --> 00:04:05,592
politely ask for the question again, for example:

64
00:04:05,592 --> 00:04:08,660
Could you repeat the question, please?

65
00:04:10,960 --> 00:04:11,528
Summary:

66
00:04:11,528 --> 00:04:15,499
rely on official sources, consolidate in the final week,

67
00:04:15,499 --> 00:04:21,173
keep to your time checkpoints for each skill, and read your band as an estimate.

68
00:04:21,173 --> 00:04:22,804
One important reminder:

69
00:04:22,804 --> 00:04:25,854
the mock test is our own shortened version,

70
00:04:25,854 --> 00:04:29,542
so the estimated band may be higher than in reality.

71
00:04:29,542 --> 00:04:33,017
The app does not guarantee your real exam result.

72
00:04:33,017 --> 00:04:34,648
Good luck on your test!
